# VVDN -- 1-HOUR MULTI-GATE DEPARTURE FLOW, RWY 35R (v2: real kinematics +
# real separation scheduling).
# 24 departures (VDN901-924, SYNTHETIC), nominal 2.5-minute pushback
# separation (pushback times may be delayed further -- see below), cycling
# through 8 real apt.dat gates (Gate 36/32/31/6/5/4/3/2, confirmed graph-
# connected to the RWY 35R area via Dijkstra) and 5 real RWY 35 SIDs.
#
# Ground-taxi kinematics: WebATM/server/taxi_kinematics.py -- an
# acceleration/deceleration-limited point-mass model (concept adopted from
# OpenTaxi, github.com/ATMRI-NTU/OpenTaxi, MIT licensed; see that module's
# docstring), NOT BlueSky's own BADA aerodynamic model, which was confirmed
# this session (live bs.sim.step() testing) to go numerically unstable
# below ~4kt. A 5kt floor is hard-coded into that module for this reason.
#
# Ground-taxi separation: WebATM/server/taxi_separation.py -- adapted from
# OpenTaxi's Opt_StopGo controller (same repo/license): aircraft are
# scheduled in pushback-priority order, and any aircraft that would come
# within 100m of an earlier (higher-priority) one on the shared taxiway
# network has its pushback delayed until clear -- this replaces a purely
# fixed-time-offset schedule, which had no actual guarantee of separation
# and was observed producing overlapping/stacked aircraft on the shared
# "E" taxiway trunk that most gates funnel into.
#
# Takeoff roll (real BADA VR: B738 140.4kt, A333 134.4kt, A320 134.5kt,
# A321 141.6kt, liftoff ~1.1NM from the real RWY 35R threshold) and SID
# climb are scripted directly (not through the separation scheduler --
# airborne aircraft have vertical/procedural separation instead), starting
# at each aircraft's ACTUAL (possibly delayed) arrival time at DEP_HOLD.
00:00:00.00>TRAILS ON
00:00:00.00>ASAS OFF

# ---- VDN901 B738 (Gate 36 -> BUNTA 2G) ----
